cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite the thesis."
title: "AWARE: A Framework for Automated Classification of Community Cultural Wealth Themes"
authors:
  - family-names: Khan
    given-names: Khalid Mehtab
type: thesis
thesis-type: "M.S. thesis"
institution:
  name: San Francisco State University
department: "Data Science and Artificial Intelligence"
year: 2026
abstract: >-
  AWARE is a framework for sentence-level multi-label classification of Community Cultural
  Wealth themes in student reflective essays. It combines domain-adaptive pre-training,
  essay-level context encoding, asymmetric loss, and per-class threshold optimization on a
  DeBERTa-v3 backbone, achieving Macro-F1 0.494 (a 30.8% improvement over a TF-IDF baseline)
  and F1 0.568-0.896 with perfect precision on single-theme sentences.
keywords:
  - multi-label text classification
  - community cultural wealth
  - educational NLP
  - DeBERTa
  - domain-adaptive pre-training
  - STEM education research
license: MIT
